# Changelog
All notable changes to the Bliss doughnut website will be documented here.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/).
This project adheres to Semantic Versioning.

## [v1.0.0] - 2026-09-18

### Added
- Initial Bliss website structure - Home, About Us, Menu, Order, Contact pages
- Responsiveness Testing section in README.md with DevTools screenshots
- Device testing evidence: Mobile (iPhone SE - 375px), Tablet (iPad Pro 13 - 1024px), Desktop (Surface Pro 10 - 1920px)
- Responsive images implementation using srcset and sizes attributes

### Fixed
- Fixed navigation menu stacking vertically on desktop view
- Fixed duplicate body selectors in style.css causing style conflicts
- Fixed image responsiveness on small screens

### Changed
- Updated README.md to include requirement 3.4 - Responsiveness testing and iteration

## [v0.1.0] - 2026-09-10
### Added
- Project proposal and initial HTML files
- Basic CSS styling and brand colors
- GitHub repository setup
# Changelog — Bliss Doughnuts Website

## Version 1.0 — Part 3 Improvements

## [v0.1.0] - 2026-10-03
###  Website Structure and Navigation

- Improved the HTML structure across the website pages.
- Made the navigation consistent across the pages.
- Corrected structural issues to improve the organisation and readability of the HTML code.

  ## [v0.1.0] - 2026-10-10
###  CSS and Website Design

- Used a separate CSS stylesheet to manage the website's appearance.
- Improved the consistency of styling across the website pages.
- Added responsive styling to improve the layout on different screen sizes.
- Improved the presentation of website content and navigation.

  ## [v0.1.0] - 2026-10-19
###  JavaScript Functionality

- Added a separate `script.js` file to keep JavaScript separate from the HTML.
- Added interactive functionality to improve the user experience.
- Implemented menu search and sorting functionality.
- Added image enlargement functionality.
- Added a mobile navigation toggle. 

  ## [v0.1.0] - 2026-10-11/12
###  Forms and Ordering

* Improved the enquiry, contact, and order forms.
* Added client-side validation to help users identify missing or invalid information.
* Added functionality to prepare an email draft containing form information.
* Added support for preselecting a product on the order page when arriving from a menu link.
* Added date restrictions to prevent selecting past delivery dates.

###  Search Engine Optimisation (SEO)

* Added canonical URL placeholders.
* Created a `robots.txt` file.
* Created a `sitemap.xml` file to help search engines discover website pages.

###  Documentation and Project Organisation

* Updated the README documentation with project information and setup instructions.
* Documented the website's features and limitations.
* Listed the image assets required by the website.

  ## [v0.1.0] - 2026-10-23
## Known Limitations

* Website images must be added to the images folder.
* Canonical URLs and sitemap details must be updated with the final published website address.
* Forms currently use client-side validation and prepare email drafts. They do not automatically store or send submissions to a database.
* The website must be tested after deployment to confirm that all pages, images, links, forms, CSS, and JavaScript work correctly.

## Future Improvements

* Connect forms to a form-processing service or backend.
* Improve accessibility and conduct further usability testing.
* Add additional product images and descriptions.
* Continue testing and improving the website based on feedback.
